# Line endings.
#
# Everything is stored and checked out with LF, including on Windows.
#
# This is not a style preference. The project is developed on Windows and
# deployed to Linux, and a Dockerfile committed with CRLF breaks the build in a
# way that gives no usable error: `RUN npm ci\r` passes the carriage return to
# npm as an argument, npm answers by printing its usage block, and the build
# fails with "npm ci did not complete successfully: exit code 1" — nothing that
# points at line endings.
#
# `bootstrap.sh` fails the same way, more obviously: a CRLF shebang makes the
# kernel look for an interpreter named `bash\r`.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary files must never be touched by any of the above.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
